  "claims": [
    {
      "text": "High-entropy alloys can have homogeneous, single-phase solid-solution structures.",
      "field": "material_initial_state",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The targeted HEAs have intrinsically random and significantly lattice-distorted microstructures.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7012927::web::018::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dynamic mechanical loading rapidly produces transient nanoscale barriers in HEAs.",
      "field": "hypothesis",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction",
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body",
        "PMC7012927::web::018::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The dynamically generated barriers may be localized short-range-ordered clusters.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Twin networks can emerge during deformation.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "entailed",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction",
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Intrinsic lattice distortions directly generate short-range order or twin networks under applied stress.",
      "field": "structural_mediator",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7012927::web::018::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Under dynamic loading, atomic-scale disorder facilitates local atomic rearrangements.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The local atomic rearrangements create temporary obstacles that pin or impede dislocation glide.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dynamically formed nanoscale barriers enhance yield strength.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body",
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Dynamically formed nanoscale barriers enhance strain hardening.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7012927::web::018::discussion",
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "The barriers permit distributed plastic flow and therefore maintain ductility while strength rises.",
      "field": "mechanism",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body",
        "PMC7012927::web::018::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the proposed controls, the tested HEA will show a statistically significant increase in yield strength.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC5321736::web::002::body",
        "PMC5893566::web::001::introduction"
      ],
      "same_system": "unclear"
    },
    {
      "text": "Relative to the proposed controls, the tested HEA will show a statistically significant increase in work-hardening rate.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "partial",
      "supporting_ids": [
        "PMC7012927::web::018::discussion"
      ],
      "same_system": "no"
    },
    {
      "text": "Serrated flow will correlate with the TEM-observed emergence of transient nanoscale barriers.",
      "field": "predicted_outcome",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "Limited thermal diffusion combined with active dislocation motion favors dynamic formation of the proposed nanoscale features.",
      "field": "conditions",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mechanism should operate over an intermediate range of temperatures and moderate-to-high strain rates.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mechanism may cease at low thermal activation because microstructural changes cannot be triggered.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The mechanism may cease at high temperatures because rapid diffusion erases transient features.",
      "field": "boundary",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
      "text": "The identity and quantitative effect of the barriers depend on alloy composition and processing history.",
      "field": "uncertainty",
      "needs_support": true,
      "support": "unsupported",
      "supporting_ids": [],
      "same_system": "na"
    },
    {
